Allocation recovery waits for the collector instead of sleeping (Strikers a9c11e0)

When a GPU-mapped allocation fails, vitaGL used to signal the garbage
collector and then sleep one second, up to FRAME_PURGE_FREQ times (a
multi-second hitch per out-of-memory event). It now enqueues a collector
cycle and waits for that cycle's completion counter (utils/gc_recovery.h,
from the Strikers port), then retries; the one-second pause is kept only as
a last chance for other threads to release memory. The CPU and GPU unsafe
allocators share one body. Semaphore/thread failures of the collector are
detected (process exit instead of a silent deadlock).
